ents an unbounded harness, not a protocol deadline.',alternatives=['Pending support is allowed to survive configuration application; the check does not demand that it be reset.','The old commit index in a returned ReadState is not an oracle failure.'])\nmg=dict(source_ids=['S_leader_other','S_read_tracking','S_joint','S_majority','S_restore_config','S_raw_read_api','S_ready_advance'],expectation_ids=['S_options','S_joint','S_read_api'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='read_support_observed records whether public Ready.ReadStates has emitted the sole context and independently computes both_majorities from an external sender-delivery ledger. The driver counts local dispatch as self participation and adds remote IDs only when it delivers actual held replies to leader Step; it never reads the implementation acknowledgment map for the oracle. For fixed incoming {1,4,5} and outgoing {1,2,3,4,5}, required counts are 2 and 3. The implication read_emitted => both_majorities is evaluated at each phase boundary. Cumulative delivered support is monotone because this measured suffix has no further reconfiguration/term change; individual read_output events record the counts at actual emission as additional diagnostics.',applicability='The phase admission follows reached committed/application joint configuration, not the observed release value. request and phase uniquely correlate phase admissions/results. Pre-joint output count, context, term, original read index and emission-time ledger counts are retained for correspondence review rather than filtered to fit the oracle.',alternatives=['Outgoing-only support may remain pending.','The both-majorities phase is a permitted positive control, not an equality or liveness oracle.'])\nplan=dict(description='Run one five-node history in which an existing read context receives no remote replies until an explicit joint voter reduction is applied. Observe self-only, one outgoing reply, outgoing-majority-only, both-majorities, and remaining-reply phases through public Ready.ReadStates and an independent delivery ledger.',claim_id=cid,binding_ids=[bid],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='TestAssuranceReadSupportAcrossJointChange: actual Bootstrap/Campaign/ReadIndex/ProposeConfChange and committed ApplyConfChange calls; delayed original heartbeat responses and public Ready output.',semantic_changes=['MemoryStorage and deterministic single-threaded FIFO local storage/transport replace production storage and scheduling; no crash or physical durability claim.','Heartbeat response delay is the sole network perturbation; messages and response contexts are not rewritten.','Read-only internal observations establish elected prefix, active configuration, applied index and unchanged term; no protocol state is assigned.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='joint_admission',event='read_phase_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='joint_applied',value=True)])],legality=legality),monitors=[dict(id='M_read_joint',checker_id='read_joint_eligibility',event='read_support_observed',binding_ids=[bid],grounding=mg,admission_alias='joint_admission',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='read_joint_eligibility',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='event',value='read_support_observed'),antecedent=dict(field='read_emitted',value=True),assertion=dict(field='both_majorities',value=True),identity_fields=['request','phase'],description='ReadState release for the sole request implies an incoming and outgoing acknowledgment majority at each fixed checkpoint. Missing either majority permits pending output.')],uncertainties=['A qualified ReadState release is not an observed client read and does not establish full linearizability.','One single-term explicit-joint voter-reduction history and five checkpoints; other reconfigurations, batching and retries remain outside this check.','Pre-joint output and emission-time diagnostics must be inspected to ensure actual release corresponds to the declared joint phase.'])\njson.dump(plan,open('read-joint-plan.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='check',rationale='Test the new read-support consumption obligation with a real committed joint transition, delayed producer replies and an independent quorum ledger.',candidate=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,rationale='Fix a necessary local eligibility condition from documented safe-read quorum and joint-majority semantics; do not equate this condition with full client linearizability.',obligation=claim,bindings=[binding]),plan_path='read-joint-plan.json',harness_path='read_joint_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S_raw_read_api','S_read_api','S_joint_selection','S_leader_other','S_restore_config','S_joint'],answered='The discriminator now has a complete producer-derived harness: initial five voters, one pending unique read, an actual committed explicit-joint reduction, and delayed heartbeat responses released in fixed order. The expected incoming/outgoing sets come from inputs and are checked against actual ConfState; the oracle does not use readOnly.acks.',remaining=['Trusted-runner execution and review must establish the actual read-output timing, support counts and control completion.','Client read endpoints and multi-request batching remain independent limits.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='Old-only support after joint application distinguishes stale request-time eligibility from current joint qualification; response 4 supplies a permitted completion control.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-read-check.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_read_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-read-check.json\"","aggregated_output":"",